{#- A path read the way it is looked for: the file's name in full, and the
    folders leading to it in grey before it, cut from their start when the room
    runs out — the end of a path is what tells two files apart. The whole of it
    stays in the tooltip. `fit`, for a column of a table: the name whole, the
    folders before it on what room the name leaves — none, if that is all
    there is — and asking the column for no more than a few words of them.
    `wrap`, where a path is read whole — a detail: all of it, broken anywhere. -#}
{%- set path = path|default('') -%}
{%- set cut = path|split('/') -%}
{%- set name = cut|last -%}
{%- set folder = cut|length > 1 ? cut|slice(0, cut|length - 1)|join('/') ~ '/' : '' -%}
<span class="file-path{{ fit|default(false) ? ' file-path--fit' }}{{ wrap|default(false) ? ' file-path--wrap' }}{{ class is defined and class ? ' ' ~ class }}" title="{{ path }}">
    {%- if folder -%}
        <span class="file-path--folder"><span dir="ltr">{{ folder }}</span></span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="file-path--name">{{ name }}</span>
</span>
